content:
An environment hook is currently intercepting and blocking all tool executions before they can run:

```
JSON hook "jsonhook__entire_PreToolUse_0_0" failed: 
Shim: Could not create process with command '"C:\Users\sahid\scoop\apps\entire\current\entire.exe" hooks antigravity pre-tool-use'
```

### 1. How to Fix the Tool Hook Error

The Scoop shim for `entire` cannot find its target executable. Run one of the following in PowerShell/Terminal:

* **If you use `entire`**: Reset or reinstall the Scoop package so the shim points to a valid binary:
  ```powershell
  scoop reset entire
  ```
  *(or `scoop install entire --force`)*

* **If you uninstalled `entire` or don't need the hook**: Remove the registered hook from your Antigravity configuration. Check:
  * `C:\Users\sahid\.gemini\antigravity\hooks.json` (or `settings.json`)
  * Remove the entry referencing `jsonhook__entire_PreToolUse_0_0` or `"entire hooks antigravity pre-tool-use"`.

Once fixed, simply reply or ask me to apply the changes directly!

---

### 2. Modern, Single-Line Responsive Quick Tags Design

To make the quick tags stay on **one single line across all screen sizes** (without awkward wrapping or overflowing), the best modern UI pattern is a **smooth horizontal scroll track with subtle scrollbar hiding, snap/fade indicators, modern pill styling, and clear visual separation** between language tags and time filters.

Here is the complete implementation you can drop into your component (e.g., `QuickTags.jsx` or `SearchBar.jsx` / `FilterBar.jsx`):

#### React Component (`QuickTags.jsx` / `QuickTags.tsx`)

```jsx
import React from 'react';
import { 
  Sparkles, 
  Code2, 
  Calendar, 
  Clock, 
  Flame 
} from 'lucide-react';

const LANGUAGE_TAGS = [
  { id: 'ai', label: 'AI', icon: Sparkles, color: 'from-purple-500/20 to-indigo-500/20 text-purple-400 border-purple-500/30 hover:border-purple-400' },
  { id: 'python', label: 'Python', icon: Code2 },
  { id: 'rust', label: 'Rust', icon: Code2 },
  { id: 'typescript', label: 'TypeScript', icon: Code2 },
  { id: 'go', label: 'Go', icon: Code2 },
];

const TIME_TAGS = [
  { id: 'today', label: 'Today', icon: Flame },
  { id: 'this-week', label: 'This Week', icon: Clock },
  { id: 'this-month', label: 'This Month', icon: Calendar },
];

export default function QuickTags({ activeTag, onSelectTag }) {
  return (
    <div className="relative w-full my-3">
      {/* Scrollable single-line container with hidden scrollbars & touch momentum */}
      <div className="flex items-center gap-2 overflow-x-auto no-scrollbar scroll-smooth py-1 px-1 -mx-1 [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_92%,transparent_100%)] sm:[mask-image:none]">

        {/* Languages & Topics */}
        <div className="flex items-center gap-1.5 shrink-0">
          {LANGUAGE_TAGS.map((tag) => {
            const Icon = tag.icon;
            const isActive = activeTag === tag.id;
            return (
              <button
                key={tag.id}
                onClick={() => onSelectTag(tag.id)}
                className={`
                  group relative inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full text-xs font-medium whitespace-nowrap
                  transition-all duration-200 select-none shrink-0
                  border backdrop-blur-md active:scale-95
                  ${isActive 
                    ? 'bg-blue-600/20 text-blue-300 border-blue-500/60 shadow-[0_0_12px_rgba(59,130,246,0.35)]' 
                    : tag.color || 'bg-slate-800/60 hover:bg-slate-700/60 text-slate-300 hover:text-white border-slate-700/60 hover:border-slate-500/60 shadow-sm'
                  }
                `}
              >
                {Icon && (
                  <Icon className={`w-3.5 h-3.5 transition-transform duration-200 group-hover:scale-110 ${isActive ? 'text-blue-400' : 'text-slate-400 group-hover:text-slate-200'}`} />
                )}
                <span>{tag.label}</span>
              </button>
            );
          })}
        </div>

        {/* Subtle vertical separator */}
        <div className="h-4 w-[1px] bg-slate-700/70 shrink-0 mx-1" />

        {/* Time filters */}
        <div className="flex items-center gap-1.5 shrink-0">
          {TIME_TAGS.map((tag) => {
            const Icon = tag.icon;
            const isActive = activeTag === tag.id;
            return (
              <button
                key={tag.id}
                onClick={() => onSelectTag(tag.id)}
                className={`
                  group relative inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full text-xs font-medium whitespace-nowrap
                  transition-all duration-200 select-none shrink-0
                  border backdrop-blur-md active:scale-95
                  ${isActive 
                    ? 'bg-amber-500/20 text-amber-300 border-amber-500/60 shadow-[0_0_12px_rgba(245,158,11,0.3)]' 
                    : 'bg-slate-800/40 hover:bg-slate-700/50 text-slate-400 hover:text-slate-200 border-slate-700/40 hover:border-slate-600/60'
                  }
                `}
              >
                {Icon && (
                  <Icon className={`w-3.5 h-3.5 transition-transform duration-200 group-hover:scale-110 ${isActive ? 'text-amber-400' : 'text-slate-500 group-hover:text-slate-300'}`} />
                )}
                <span>{tag.label}</span>
              </button>
            );
          })}
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  );
}
```

#### Tailwind / CSS Helper for hiding scrollbars:
If not already present in your CSS, add this utility to `index.css`:
```css
@layer utilities {
  .no-scrollbar::-webkit-scrollbar {
    display: none;
  }
  .no-scrollbar {
    -ms-overflow-style: none;
    scrollbar-width: none;
  }
}
```

### Key Design Upgrades:
1. **Guaranteed Single-Line & Mobile Responsive**: `whitespace-nowrap`, `shrink-0`, and `overflow-x-auto` allow smooth kinetic swipe on touchscreens while never wrapping into multiple lines.
2. **Right Edge Fade**: `[mask-image:linear-gradient(...)]` on mobile naturally indicates more tags are scrollable without needing an ugly scrollbar.
3. **Visual Hierarchy**: A divider separates content types (languages vs. time spans) with custom accent colors (AI gets a purple highlight, time filters get subtle amber highlights).
4. **Micro-interactions**: Hover scaling, click bounce (`active:scale-95`), and soft glow rings for selected tags.

